  "limitations": [
    "These games postdate original Gen37 training but are a selected convenience corpus, not a preregistered independent benchmark.",
    "Games came from the canonical Gen38 data-generation run with neutral-prepared Gen37 and a frozen-opponent mixture; recovery/completion filters limit generalization.",
    "Only Play-phase positions with at least one hidden opponent dev card are included.",
    "The training value target mixes35% game result with65% search estimate, so raw values are not calibrated win probabilities.",
    "Examples shown in the blog are illustrations selected by score, not a representative performance sample.",
    "Implied probabilities use only the fixed algebraic transform; no calibration parameters are fitted.",
    "Brier skill is a proper-score comparison on these recorded outcomes; the empirical constant baseline is retrospective, not a deployed or separately trained forecast.",
    "Binned R\u00b2 suppresses individual binary-outcome noise and should not be interpreted as the fraction of per-position outcomes explained.",
    "Calibration is a property of predicted probabilities and observed frequencies under these continuation policies; it does not establish causality or opening calibration.",
    "The same game can contribute positions to multiple bins. Counts of contributing games across bins must not be added."
  ],
